# Strip .html extension with a 301 permanent redirect
# (so Google drops the old .html URLs from its index)
#
# NOTE: domain-level sources (e.g. https://www.example.com/*) are NOT supported
# in Cloudflare Pages _redirects. The www -> non-www redirect is handled by a
# Cloudflare Page Rule at the edge instead, which runs before Pages.
/*.html  /:splat  301

# /tools is the obvious guess on a site where every tool lives under /tools/,
# and it 404s because there is no directory index there — the tools are listed
# on the homepage. Nothing internal links to these, but people type them and
# Googlebot follows them from elsewhere.
/tools      /  301
/tools/     /  301
/tool       /  301
/all-tools  /  301
/sitemap    /sitemap.xml  301
